    "rawMarkdown": "# Day 18: Kubernetes Resource Management - Requests, Limits, LimitRange & Quotas\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccc Course & Topic Overview\n- **Course:** Docker & Kubernetes (KR Network Cloud)\n- **Module:** Kubernetes Compute Resource Management & Governance\n- **Key Concepts:** `requests` vs `limits`, Compressible vs Incompressible Resources, OOMKilled (Exit Code 137), CPU Throttling (CFS), `LimitRange`, `ResourceQuota`, Metrics Server & `kubectl top`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Units of Compute: Millicores & Mebibytes\n\n- **CPU Units (Millicores - `m`):** Expressed in millicores (`m`). 1 vCPU / Core = 1000m. Therefore, `250m` equals 0.25 of a CPU core.\n- **Memory Units (Bytes / Mebibytes - `Mi`/`Gi`):** Expressed in binary power-of-two mebibytes (`Mi`) or gibibytes (`Gi`). 1Gi = 1024Mi.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Deep Dive: `requests` vs `limits` & OOMKilled Mechanics\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    Pod[\"Pod with Resources:<br/>requests: memory=256Mi, cpu=200m<br/>limits: memory=512Mi, cpu=500m\"]\n    Pod --> Sched[\"kube-scheduler\"]\n    Sched -->|Checks Requests ONLY| Node[\"Worker Node with Free Capacity\"]\n    Node --> Run[\"Pod Starts Running\"]\n    Run --> OverCPU[\"Container attempts 600m CPU\"]\n    OverCPU --> Throttle[\"Linux CFS Throttles CPU<br/>(Slows down, NO Crash)\"]\n    Run --> OverMem[\"Container attempts 550Mi RAM\"]\n    OverMem --> OOM[\"Kernel Out-Of-Memory Killer<br/>OOMKilled (Exit Code 137)!\"]\n```\n\n| Resource Type | Behavior When Exceeding `requests` | Behavior When Exceeding `limits` |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CPU (Compressible)** | Allowed to burst into unreserved node capacity. | Throttled by Linux Completely Fair Scheduler (CFS). Pod continues running. |\n| **Memory (Incompressible)** | Allowed to consume up to limit if node has free memory. | Process is terminated immediately by Linux OOM killer (`OOMKilled` - Exit Code 137). |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Production Pod Manifest with Resource Constraints\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: secured-api\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: api\n    image: nginx:alpine\n    resources:\n      requests:\n        memory: \"128Mi\"\n        cpu: \"100m\"\n      limits:\n        memory: \"256Mi\"\n        cpu: \"250m\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. LimitRange: Default & Boundary Enforcement\n\nEnforces default resource boundaries across containers in a namespace, preventing unconstrained runaway pods:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: LimitRange\nmetadata:\n  name: default-container-limits\n  namespace: development\nspec:\n  limits:\n  - default:              # Default LIMIT if developer omits it\n      cpu: \"500m\"\n      memory: \"512Mi\"\n    defaultRequest:       # Default REQUEST if developer omits it\n      cpu: \"100m\"\n      memory: \"128Mi\"\n    max:                  # Max allowed limit\n      cpu: \"1000m\"\n      memory: \"1Gi\"\n    min:                  # Min allowed request\n      cpu: \"50m\"\n      memory: \"64Mi\"\n    type: Container\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. ResourceQuota: Multi-Tenant Namespace Governance\n\nRestricts aggregate resource consumption across an entire namespace:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ResourceQuota\nmetadata:\n  name: team-quota\n  namespace: development\nspec:\n  hard:\n    requests.cpu: \"4\"\n    requests.memory: \"8Gi\"\n    limits.cpu: \"8\"\n    limits.memory: \"16Gi\"\n    pods: \"20\"\n    services: \"10\"\n    services.loadbalancers: \"1\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Metrics Server & Cluster Observability\n\n```bash\n# Install Metrics Server on cluster\nkubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml\n\n# Monitor live CPU and RAM consumption across nodes\nkubectl top nodes\n\n# Monitor live CPU and RAM consumption across pods in a namespace\nkubectl top pods -n development\n\n# View pod sorted by memory consumption\nkubectl top pods -A --sort-by=memory\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Day 18 Review & Interview Questions\n\n1. **What is the fundamental difference between resource requests and limits?**\n   - `requests` represent the guaranteed minimum resources reserved by the scheduler during node placement. `limits` represent the hard ceiling a container cannot exceed at runtime.\n2. **What causes a Pod to terminate with 'Exit Code 137' (OOMKilled)?**\n   - Exit Code 137 indicates that the Linux Out-Of-Memory (OOM) killer terminated the container process because its RAM usage exceeded the configured memory limit (or node memory ran out).\n3. **What is the difference between a LimitRange and a ResourceQuota?**\n   - `LimitRange` sets boundaries and default values on individual containers/pods. `ResourceQuota` sets aggregate hard ceilings across the entire namespace as a whole.\n4. **What happens if a developer attempts to create a Pod without resource limits in a namespace governed by a ResourceQuota?**\n   - If a ResourceQuota is applied to a namespace, Kubernetes admission control will REJECT any pod creation request that lacks explicit resource requests/limits (unless a LimitRange provides default values).\n",
    "mermaid": "graph TD\n    Pod[\"Pod with Resources:<br/>requests: memory=256Mi, cpu=200m<br/>limits: memory=512Mi, cpu=500m\"]\n    Pod --> Sched[\"kube-scheduler\"]\n    Sched -->|Checks Requests ONLY| Node[\"Worker Node with Free Capacity\"]\n    Node --> Run[\"Pod Starts Running\"]\n    Run --> OverCPU[\"Container attempts 600m CPU\"]\n    OverCPU --> Throttle[\"Linux CFS Throttles CPU<br/>(Slows down, NO Crash)\"]\n    Run --> OverMem[\"Container attempts 550Mi RAM\"]\n    OverMem --> OOM[\"Kernel Out-Of-Memory Killer<br/>OOMKilled (Exit Code 137)!\"]",
    "commands": "# YAML\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: secured-api\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: api\n    image: nginx:alpine\n    resources:\n      requests:\n        memory: \"128Mi\"\n        cpu: \"100m\"\n      limits:\n        memory: \"256Mi\"\n        cpu: \"250m\"\n\n# YAML\napiVersion: v1\nkind: LimitRange\nmetadata:\n  name: default-container-limits\n  namespace: development\nspec:\n  limits:\n  - default:              # Default LIMIT if developer omits it\n      cpu: \"500m\"\n      memory: \"512Mi\"\n    defaultRequest:       # Default REQUEST if developer omits it\n      cpu: \"100m\"\n      memory: \"128Mi\"\n    max:                  # Max allowed limit\n      cpu: \"1000m\"\n      memory: \"1Gi\"\n    min:                  # Min allowed request\n      cpu: \"50m\"\n      memory: \"64Mi\"\n    type: Container\n\n# YAML\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ResourceQuota\nmetadata:\n  name: team-quota\n  namespace: development\nspec:\n  hard:\n    requests.cpu: \"4\"\n    requests.memory: \"8Gi\"\n    limits.cpu: \"8\"\n    limits.memory: \"16Gi\"\n    pods: \"20\"\n    services: \"10\"\n    services.loadbalancers: \"1\"",
