    "title": "Day 24: Kubernetes Persistent Storage - Volumes, PV, PVC, StorageClasses & Dynamic Provisioning",
    "cleanTitle": "Kubernetes Persistent Storage - Volumes, PV, PVC, StorageClasses & Dynamic Provisioning",
    "duration": "1h 45m",
    "moduleId": 9,
    "moduleName": "Module 9: Decoupled Configuration & Clustered Storage",
    "moduleBadge": "Config & StatefulSets",
    "color": "#F97316",
    "icon": "database",
    "rawMarkdown": "# Day 24: Kubernetes Persistent Storage - Volumes, PV, PVC, StorageClasses & Dynamic Provisioning\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccc Course & Topic Overview\n- **Course:** Docker & Kubernetes (KR Network Cloud)\n- **Module:** Kubernetes Storage Architecture & Volume Provisioning\n- **Key Concepts:** Ephemeral Volumes (`emptyDir`, `hostPath`), Network Persistent Storage, PersistentVolumes (PV), PersistentVolumeClaims (PVC), AccessModes (`RWO`, `ROX`, `RWX`, `RWOP`), Reclaim Policies (`Retain`, `Delete`), Static Provisioning (NFS), Dynamic Provisioning (`StorageClass`, AWS EBS CSI, `allowVolumeExpansion`), and `WaitForFirstConsumer`\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Storage Abstraction: Ephemeral vs Persistent\n\n- **`emptyDir`:** Temporary scratch disk scoped to the Pod lifespan; destroyed upon pod deletion.\n- **`hostPath`:** Mounts a local directory from the host worker node; single point of failure if rescheduled.\n- **`PV / PVC`:** Decoupled network-attached storage (NFS, AWS EBS, Ceph) that follows workloads across nodes.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture of the PV, PVC & StorageClass Binding Lifecycle\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    Dev[\"Developer\"] -->|Submits PVC Manifest<br/>requests: 5Gi, RWO| PVC[\"PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)<br/>(Namespace Scoped)\"]\n    PVC -->|Finds matching or triggers| SC[\"StorageClass<br/>(Dynamic Provisioner)\"]\n    SC -->|Calls Cloud API / Provisioner| Storage[\"Cloud Disk (AWS EBS / NFS)\"]\n    Storage -->|Creates and Binds| PV[\"PersistentVolume (PV)<br/>(Cluster Scoped)\"]\n    PV <==>|Bound State| PVC\n    Pod[\"Application Pod\"] -->|Mounts Volume| PVC\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. AccessModes & Reclaim Policies Deep Dive\n\n| Access Mode | CLI Abbreviation | Description / Permitted Concurrency |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`ReadWriteOnce`** | `RWO` | Volume can be mounted as read-write by a SINGLE node. |\n| **`ReadOnlyMany`** | `ROX` | Volume can be mounted read-only by MANY nodes simultaneously. |\n| **`ReadWriteMany`** | `RWX` | Volume can be mounted as read-write by MANY nodes (e.g. NFS, Ceph, EFS). |\n| **`ReadWriteOncePod`**| `RWOP`| Volume can be mounted as read-write by a SINGLE Pod across the cluster. |\n\n| Reclaim Policy | Action When PVC is Deleted | Data Safety |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`Retain` (Manual default)** | PV enters 'Released' state; physical volume and data are preserved intact. | Maximum Safety (Manual admin intervention). |\n| **`Delete` (StorageClass default)** | Associated PV and underlying cloud disk (AWS EBS) are deleted immediately. | Cost-efficient for dev clusters; destructive for DBs. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Static Provisioning Lab Blueprint (NFS + PV + PVC)\n\n```yaml\n# Step 1: Cluster-wide PV pointing to NFS Server\napiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolume\nmetadata:\n  name: nfs-pv-5gb\nspec:\n  capacity:\n    storage: 5Gi\n  volumeMode: Filesystem\n  accessModes:\n    - ReadWriteMany\n  persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain\n  storageClassName: manual\n  mountOptions:\n    - hard\n    - nfsvers=4.1\n  nfs:\n    path: /data/exports\n    server: 192.168.30.35\n---\n# Step 2: Namespace-scoped PVC requesting storage\napiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: nfs-app-pvc\n  namespace: production\nspec:\n  accessModes:\n    - ReadWriteMany\n  storageClassName: manual\n  resources:\n    requests:\n      storage: 5Gi\n---\n# Step 3: Deployment consuming PVC\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: shared-web-app\n  namespace: production\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: web\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: web\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: nginx\n        image: nginx:alpine\n        volumeMounts:\n        - name: app-storage\n          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html\n      volumes:\n      - name: app-storage\n        persistentVolumeClaim:\n          claimName: nfs-app-pvc\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Dynamic Provisioning Lab Blueprint (StorageClass)\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1\nkind: StorageClass\nmetadata:\n  name: fast-ebs-sc\nprovisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com   # AWS EBS CSI Driver\nvolumeBindingMode: WaitForFirstConsumer\nallowVolumeExpansion: true\nparameters:\n  type: gp3\n  iops: \"3000\"\n  throughput: \"125\"\n---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: dynamic-db-pvc\n  namespace: production\nspec:\n  accessModes:\n    - ReadWriteOnce\n  storageClassName: fast-ebs-sc\n  resources:\n    requests:\n      storage: 20Gi\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification & Troubleshooting Commands\n\n```bash\n# View PV, PVC and StorageClasses\nkubectl get pv\nkubectl get pvc -A\nkubectl get sc\n\n# Inspect pending PVC\nkubectl describe pvc dynamic-db-pvc -n production\n\n# Online volume expansion\nkubectl patch pvc dynamic-db-pvc -n production -p '{\"spec\":{\"resources\":{\"requests\":{\"storage\":\"40Gi\"}}}}'\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Day 24 Review & Interview Questions\n\n1. **What is the difference between a PersistentVolume (PV) and a PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)?**\n   - A PersistentVolume (PV) is a cluster-scoped resource representing physical/cloud storage provisioned by an administrator or StorageClass. A PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) is a namespace-scoped request by a developer for a specific amount and access mode of storage.\n2. **Why would a PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) get stuck in 'Pending' state?**\n   - A PVC will remain stuck in 'Pending' if: (1) No existing PV matches its capacity, AccessModes, and storageClassName; (2) The dynamic provisioner plugin/CSI driver is not functioning; or (3) volumeBindingMode is set to 'WaitForFirstConsumer' and no Pod referencing the PVC has been scheduled yet.\n3. **Why can't an AWS EBS volume support 'ReadWriteMany' (RWX)?**\n   - Standard block storage volumes like AWS EBS gp2/gp3 are physically attached to a single virtual machine hypervisor at a time, meaning only pods on that specific node can mount it (RWO). Shared filesystems like NFS, AWS EFS, or CephFS allow multi-node concurrent read/write (RWX).\n4. **What happens to the data on a PV when a PVC with 'persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain' is deleted?**\n   - Under 'Retain', the PV enters 'Released' state. Its data and underlying storage volume remain completely intact and untouched. An administrator must manually inspect the data, delete the PV, and reclaim the physical disk.\n",
    "mermaid": "graph TD\n    Dev[\"Developer\"] -->|Submits PVC Manifest<br/>requests: 5Gi, RWO| PVC[\"PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)<br/>(Namespace Scoped)\"]\n    PVC -->|Finds matching or triggers| SC[\"StorageClass<br/>(Dynamic Provisioner)\"]\n    SC -->|Calls Cloud API / Provisioner| Storage[\"Cloud Disk (AWS EBS / NFS)\"]\n    Storage -->|Creates and Binds| PV[\"PersistentVolume (PV)<br/>(Cluster Scoped)\"]\n    PV <==>|Bound State| PVC\n    Pod[\"Application Pod\"] -->|Mounts Volume| PVC",
